.\" Manpage for NX CLI
.TH NX 1 "03 September 2026" "1.0.0" "NX Manual"
.SH NAME
nx \- Autonomous Nuxt module scaffolder & project wrapper
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./nx
[\fIOPTION\fR] [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nx
is a cross-platform CLI tool for Nuxt 3/4 applications. It allows creating pre-configured Nuxt applications with Tailwind CSS, scaffolding autonomous modules, importing distant GitHub modules into a central registry (\fBnx.config.json\fR), and publishing module updates.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B create \fIPROJECT_NAME\fR
Scaffold a new Nuxt 3/4 project pre-configured with Tailwind CSS, \fBnx.config.json\fR, and an embedded \fB./nx\fR wrapper.
.TP
.B \-m, \-\-module \fIMODULE_NAME\fR
Scaffold a local feature module in \fB./modules/MODULE_NAME\fR within an existing Nuxt project.
.TP
.B \-i, \-\-import [\fIURL_OR_NAME\fR]
Import remote module(s) from a GitHub repository or sync all modules defined in \fBnx.config.json\fR.
.TP
.B \-u, \-\-update [\fIMODULE_NAME\fR]
Fetch and pull the latest Git changes for a specific module or all imported modules.
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-push [\fIMODULE_NAME\fR] [\fICOMMIT_MESSAGE\fR]
Commit and push local modifications of a specific module (or all modified modules) back to GitHub.
.TP
.B \-l, \-\-list
List all installed modules in the project with their Git status, branch, and remote URL.
.TP
.B man, \-\-man
Display this manual page.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display formatted command-line help message.
.SH FILES
.I nx.config.json
Central module registry storing module names, GitHub URLs, and branches.
